{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "duo_extend",
    "description": "Halo extension of a cell field into the 3-layer donor-cube halo (Mouallem et al. duo-grid). The interior copy is region 0; each of the 24 tile-edge strips applies a shared per-edge remap template (duo_extend_strip_{w,e,s,n}): a tent-basis (bilinear) interpolation in the donor tile's gnomonic coordinates X, Y with one-sided linear extrapolation past the donor edge. X and Y are bound per strip as the signed face-rotation of the halo cell's Cartesian center into the donor frame; dt is the donor tile.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:duo",
      "op:halo_extend",
      "order:2",
      "bc:duo",
      "axes:tile,x_cell_ext,y_cell_ext",
      "form:remap",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Chen, X. (2021). The LMARS based shallow-water dynamical core on generic gnomonic cubed-sphere geometry. JAMES, 13, e2020MS002280. https://doi.org/10.1029/2020MS002280"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/duo_extend_strip_e.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/duo_extend_strip_n.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/duo_extend_strip_s.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/duo_extend_strip_w.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "duo_extend": {
      "params": [
        "q",
        "center",
        "refx",
        "refy"
      ],
      "description": "Fill the 3-layer halo of an A-grid field q[tile, x, y] from the NEIGHBOUR tiles, giving qext[tile, x_cell_ext, y_cell_ext] -- the duo-grid remap that is the whole point of this grid (the paper's 'duo' is the two coexisting halo point sets). Every halo cell centre is a known sphere point from the tile's OWN extended geometry (bind `center` to duo_cell_center); it is mapped into the DONOR tile's cube frame by the closed-form signed component ratio of duo_tile_map (X = signX s[dX] / (signf s[f0]), verified to 1e-16 against the linear solve), and the donor field is sampled there by a TENSOR-PRODUCT TENT (exact piecewise-linear) over the donor cell-centre cube coordinates 0.5(ref[k]+ref[k+1]) (bind `refx`/`refy` to the same reference lines as duo_node_cart). The donor field is padded by ONE linear-extrapolation ghost cell each side (2 q1 - q2 at the low edge, 2 qN - q(N-1) at the high edge) so the outermost halo layer -- which maps just past the donor's last cell centre -- stays bracketed by two knots; without it the equi-edge and equidistance grids drop to O(h) there. The tent has COMPACT SUPPORT, so summing over the full donor sweep k,l in 0..N+1 needs no search and no window: the weight is identically zero outside the two bracketing knots, and clamped gathers keep every donor access in [1,N] regardless of which ifelse ghost branch is live. STRUCTURE: a makearray whose first region is a whole-box base fill (q gathered with the ext->local shift and a clamp -- exact in the interior, a placeholder in the halo) and whose 24 further regions (6 tiles x 4 sides, donor pinned per region from the staircase table NB) OVERWRITE the W/E/S/N halo strips with the tent contraction; the four corner blocks per tile are never read by the direction-split 1-D reconstructions and keep the base fill. ACCURACY vs the paper: this is the bilinear donor-cube remap, not the paper's section-2.3 1-D-mirror construction; it matches the paper's stated (non-critical) remap accuracy and, unlike direct reference-line extension, is genuinely second order on ALL three projections (measured max halo error 3.0e-3/4.2e-3/3.8e-3 at N=16 -> 2.0e-4/1.7e-4/1.6e-4 at N=64 for equiangular/equi-edge/equidistance, rate ~2, over all 24 seams). COST NOTE: the full 0..N+1 sweep is O(N^2) weight evaluations per halo cell; the weights are pure geometry and fold at a binding site, but a consumer wanting the runtime win can replace the sweep with a closed-form bracket (atan inversion of the reference line) plus a fixed +-2 window without changing any result.",
